  reason: "WHY RUST IS STILL NEEDED, and it is the bootstrap constraint rather than seed-shrink debt: this decides whether resolving the corpus may BEGIN, so it cannot be a value obtained by resolving the corpus. whole_corpus_compile_seed_mirror_note argues that at length and binds this growth to the dissolution the sibling mirrors already specify rather than authoring a fourth.\n\nWHY IT IS ADMITTED AGAINST THE v1 FREEZE: gunbc.v1_maintenance_standing v1_seed_standing admits a change by PURPOSE — it serves the v2 self-host program. The instrument this refusal guards, gunbc compile --target dag over both source roots, IS the self-emission instrument, and it was OOM-killed into a silent exit-137 zero. This is defect repair on the self-host path, not growth of the seed for its own sake.\n\nHAND-ITEM DELTA: +7, all citable above, enumerated rather than counted from what was touched — the method stage0_rust_observation_seed_growth_justification records having got wrong twice. Four are production (the demand constant, the admission coproduct, the fold over it, the refusal renderer) and three are the tests that discriminate it. HAND-LOC DELTA: +173 in memory_governor.rs and +29 in main.rs against origin/main, a large share of it the doc comments carrying the receipts and the refusal strings.\n\nNO NEW UNCITABLE ITEM, DELIBERATELY. whole_corpus_compile_refusal_diagnostic is a free function and not an inherent method on WholeCorpusCompileAdmission, because DeclField offers WholeDeclaration or NamedField and neither names a method on an impl block. The sibling receipt carries one such item in prose only because its Display realization had no citable form; this one had a citable form available and takes it rather than growing that class.\n\nWHAT IS NOT GROWTH AND IS NOT LISTED: the main.rs join itself. It adds no declaration — it is an arm inside the existing Compile match, so its disposition is ExistingSeedItemModified, and listing it would net a modification into an addition census.",
